Data lineage and licensing
--------------------------

The drive-level dataset shipped at `data/drives.csv` (and its `.rds`
counterpart) is a derivative of public play-by-play data distributed via the
`nflfastR` R package, maintained by Sebastian Carl and Ben Baldwin.
`nflfastR` itself is MIT-licensed and extends the original `nflscrapR`
pipeline of Yurko, Ventura, and Horowitz (2018), also MIT-licensed.

The underlying play-by-play records originate from publicly broadcast NFL
games. No proprietary or licensed feeds (e.g., NFL Next Gen Stats, Pro
Football Focus) are used.

Re-distribution of the derived `drives.csv` here is consistent with the
upstream MIT terms.
